  "id": "zhuang_shange_antiphonal",
  "name": "Zhuang shan'ge (Guangxi antiphonal song-fair singing)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sung-verse culture of the Zhuang of Guangxi, in which young men and women trade memorised and improvised verses in antiphonal exchange at seasonal song fairs (gexu), the largest around the third day of the third lunar month; the legendary singer Liu Sanjie personifies the tradition. In Mashan and neighbouring counties the Zhuang also sing two- and three-part songs, listed with other multipart folk songs on China's national intangible-heritage register.",
  "recipe": "classic modern zhuang shan'ge, ballad Poetry, vocal drone modal. leader call answered, two spatially opposed choirs, single lead single track no stacking. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
